<%= header(1, 'What is this?') %>
<%= erb :description %>

<ol>
  <li>Every game save has a <strong>seed</strong> number used to calculate the rolling result.</li>
  <li>The seed number will only change if you roll the rare gacha.</li>
  <li>We can observe the rolling results and figure out your seed for your game save.</li>
  <li>The simulator is able to use the seed to calculate all the future rolling results.</li>
</ol>

<%= header(1, 'Frequently asked questions') %>
<ol>
  <li>
    Will I ever need to find my seed a second time?
    <ul>
      <li>No, <strong>you only need to find your seed once</strong>. Your seed will never change without rolling, and you can <a href="#advancing-the-tracks">update it as you roll</a> in the game.</li>
      <li>All events including platinum and legend ones share the same seed.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    Can I go backward in my track?
    <ul>
      <li>No, your tracks can only be advanced forward.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><a href="#switching-tracks">How can I switch to the other track</a>?</li>
  <li>
    When will my tracks shuffle, or seed reset?
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your tracks and seed will never shuffle or reset</strong>. Your tracks will only change when you select a different event, and the same banner comes in the future are different events.</li>
      <li>The ubers in the uber positions can change when a new uber is added to the banner. Likewise, the legends in the legend positions can change when the banner has multiple legends.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    Why the color sometimes doesn't match with the cat's rarity?
    <ul>
      <li>Colors are fixed at the positions to help you discover across events, and they're not meant to indicate the rarity of the cats. To also indicate the rarity of the cats, use <a href="#advanced-highlighting">advanced highlighting.</a></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<%= header(1, 'How to use') %>
<p class="section">
  First, you'll want to find your current seed. Watch the video or read the text explanation.
</p>

<%= header(2, %Q{<a href="#{route.seek_uri}">Seeking the seed</a>}) %>
<p style="width: 640px; height: 360px"><iframe src="https://streamable.com/s/02nrn/pmxcpt" frameborder="0" width="100%" height="100%" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>

<ol>
  <li>
    Before you hit <em>seek</em>, follow these steps: <%= erb :help_seek %>
  </li>
  <li>
    Understand the results: <%= erb :help_seek_result %>
  </li>
</ol>

<%= header(2, 'Reading the tracks') %>
<ul>
  <li>Using the link from the seek result, you'll see a table looks like below.</li>
  <li>Suppose you start at <strong>1A</strong>, then your next roll with rare ticket or cat food will be the cat located in 1A. It's a rare cat (<strong>1A rare cat</strong>) in this case.</li>
  <li>Your next roll will be located at <strong>2A</strong>, which is a super rare cat (<span class="supa">2A supa cat</span>).</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].mark_next_position(arg[:help].read_the_tracks) %>

<%= header(2, 'Highlighting rolls') %>
<ul>
  <li>You can click on the cells, and it'll highlight the cats you'll roll out.</li>
  <li>Suppose we click on <span class="supa">2A supa cat</span>'s cell, and 2A + 3A will be <span class="picked">highlighted</span> in light grey.</li>
  <li><strong>3A rare cat</strong> will also be <span class="next_position">highlighted</span> in stripes, indicating your next position after the rolls.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].read_the_tracks, 2, 0) %>

<%= header(2, 'Advancing the tracks') %>
<ul>
  <li>You can click on the cat's name, which will simulate that you rolled to that cat.</li>
  <li>Following the above example, let's click on the cat's name at 2A (i.e. <span class="supa">2A supa cat</span>) to simulate that you rolled to that cat. This will lead you to a table looks like below.</li>
  <li>You can see that you advanced two rows. Previously <strong>3A rare cat</strong> was located at 3A, <span class="next_position">highlighted</span> in stripes, now it's located at 1A.</li>
  <li>Your new next roll will be <strong>3A rare cat</strong> located at <strong>1A</strong>.</li>
  <li>You can see that the other track will also advance, meaning that you can only pick one in the same row.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].mark_next_position(arg[:help].advance_the_tracks) %>

<%= header(2, "Looking up cat's data") %>
<ul>
  <li>You can click on <strong>🐾</strong> beside the cat's name, which will show you the cat's data.</li>
  <li>If <strong>🐾</strong> isn't showing up, click on the cat's name instead.</li>
</ul>
<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].lookup_cat_data %>

<%= header(2, 'What is a guaranteed event') %>
<ul>
  <li>There are two kinds of guaranteed events.</li>
  <li>One is 11 continuous rolls with 1500 cat food, which the 11st roll will be 100% uber regardless previous rolls, meaning that even if you rolled an uber cat earlier, the 11st will still be an uber cat.</li>
  <li>The other one is 3+5+7 (15) step up events, or increasing capsules, which you first use 300 cat food to roll 3 times continuously, and then 750 cat food to roll 5 times continuously, and finally 1050 cat food to roll 7 times continuously. In total 15 (3+5+7) rolls. Similar to 11 rolls guaranteed events, the last 15th roll will be 100% uber.</li>
  <li>Platinum gacha with platinum tickets for 100% uber <strong>IS NOT</strong> a guaranteed event. Only 11 rolls or 15 rolls can be a guaranteed event.</li>
</ul>

<%= header(2, 'What is a guaranteed uber') %>
<ul>
  <li>A guaranteed uber is the last roll with 11 or 15 rolls in a guaranteed event.</li>
  <li>Even if you rolled an uber as the last roll, if it's not rolled in a guaranteed event, it's not a guaranteed uber.</li>
  <li>An uber from platinum or legend event is not a guaranteed uber.</li>
</ul>

<%= header(2, 'Reading the guaranteed tracks') %>
<ul>
  <li>Ubers listed on the guaranteed column are the guaranteed ubers.</li>
  <li>Guaranteed ubers will only be displayed if we're looking at a guaranteed event.</li>
  <li>Here if you make 11 guaranteed rolls, you'll get 1A ~ 10A and lastly <strong>1A guaranteed uber</strong> (1AG), totally 11 cats.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].mark_next_position(arg[:help].guaranteed_tracks) %>

<%= header(2, 'Highlighting guaranteed rolls') %>
<ul>
  <li>You can also click on the guaranteed cells, and all the cats you'll roll out will be highlighted.</li>
  <li>Here we click on <strong>1A guaranteed uber</strong>'s cell, and 1A ~ 10A + 1A guaranteed uber (1AG) are <span class="picked_consecutively">highlighted</span> in dark grey.</li>
  <li><strong>11B</strong> will also be <span class="next_position">highlighted</span> in stripes, indicating your next position after the 11 rolls.</li>
  <li>This is also indicated on the 1A guaranteed uber's cell, shown as <em>-&gt; 11B</em>. Here we jump from 1A to 11B.</li>
  <li>This will lead to the next topic: <a href="#switching-tracks">Switching tracks</a>.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].guaranteed_tracks, 1, 0, true) %>

<%= header(2, 'Switching tracks') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    There are two cases that you will switch between the tracks:
    <ol>
      <li>
        Performing guaranteed rolls in a <a href="#what-is-a-guaranteed-event">guaranteed event</a>. Note that platinum gacha <strong>IS NOT</strong> a guaranteed event.
      </li>
      <li>
        Rolling a potentially <a href="#consecutive-duplicated-rare-cats">consecutive duplicated rare cat</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>
    Beside that you always stay on the same track, regardless you're seeing it
    as track A or B. <a href="#tracks-are-perspective">Tracks are perspective</a>.
  </li>
  <li>Here's an example switching from B to A.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].guaranteed_tracks, 1, 1, true) %>

<%= header(2, 'Tracks are perspective') %>
<ul>
  <li>Track A or B is purely perspective. You're always on track A, and the other track is the alternative track.</li>
  <li>To observe the perspective, let's look at this example. Suppose we click on <strong>2B rare cat</strong>'s cell, highlighting the rolls:</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].read_the_tracks, 2, 1) %>

<ul>
  <li>And then we click on <strong>2B rare cat</strong>'s name to roll to that position.</li>
  <li>We'll see that now the previous track B swapped to A, and A swapped to B.</li>
  <li>You're staying on the same track, because the next roll is still <span class="uber">3B uber cat</span> and so on, but the perspective is changed and swapped.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].mark_next_position(arg[:help].swap_the_tracks) %>

<%= header(2, 'Consecutive duplicated rare cats') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    The game does not allow you to get two consecutive duplicated rare cats
    in a row. Whenever you could be getting a consecutive duplicated rare cat,
    instead of giving you that, the game will instead make an additional
    half roll, to roll another rare cat for you.
  </li>
  <li>
    As a result, <strong>it'll move you to the other track</strong> upon
    hitting into a consecutive duplicated rare cat, and you'll get a different
    rare cat which is different than the previous one you got, based on the
    result of this additional half roll.
  </li>
  <li>
    The reason you'll switch to the other track is exactly the same as rolling
    a guaranteed uber cat, that it'll make a half roll, and
    <a href="#switching-track-is-the-effect-of-making-a-half-roll">switching track is the effect of making a half roll</a>.
  </li>
  <li>Let's look at an example where we have a consecutive duplicated rare cat at <strong>4A</strong>, a Tin Cat can turn into a <strong>Pogo Cat</strong>.</li>
  <li>Assuming you're clicking on the cell for 4A, highlighting the path toward it.</li>
  <li>You'll see that Pogo Cat was highlighted rather than the Tin Cat, and your next position will jump to <strong>5B</strong> instead of 5A.</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].dupe_rare_tracks, 4, 0) %>

<%= header(2, 'Bouncing with consecutive duplicated rare cats') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    It is not very common but it's possible that you could immediately get
    another duplicated rare cat right after you switched to the other track.
  </li>
  <li>
    When this happens, as you would expect, the same mechanism will kick in
    and you would get another re-rolled rare cat and switch the track again.
  </li>
  <li>
    Here's an example showing 3A -&gt; 4AR (4A re-rolled) -&gt;
    5BR (5B re-rolled) -&gt; 7A
  </li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].bouncing_tracks, 4, 0) %>

<%= header(2, 'Not necessarily a consecutive duplicated rare cat') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    Did you notice that in the above example, while 4B and 5B are different
    rare cats, the track still shows a re-rolled cat at 5B? That's used
    when you're coming from 4AR, but what if you're coming from 4B?
  </li>
  <li>
    Remember again that the game will only re-roll a rare cat for you
    if and only if you could get a consecutive duplicated rare cat.
    It is not depending on the tracks themselves. Those are not fixed.
    It's fully depending on what exactly was the last cat you got,
    <a href="#hidden-track-switches-between-events"><strong>even across the events</strong></a>!
  </li>
  <li>
    Here's an example showing you coming from 4B so 5B is not a consecutive
    duplicated rare cat, therefore you'll go through it without switching to
    the other track.
  </li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].go_straight_tracks, 7, 1) %>

<%= header(2, 'Dodging consecutive duplicated rare cat with a platinum or legend ticket') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    Remember again that the game will only re-roll a rare cat for you
    if and only if you could get a consecutive duplicated rare cat.
  </li>
  <li>
    What if you get an uber or legend in place of one of the consecutive
    duplicated rare cats, at 3A or 4A? You will avoid getting consecutive
    duplicated rare cats, therefore you will not switch to the other track.
  </li>
  <li>Example that we got Nekoluga at 3A with a platinum ticket, replacing the original Tin Cat, and we will not switch:</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].dodge_dupes_3a, 4, 0) %>

<ul>
  <li>Example that we got Marauder Cat at 4A with a platinum ticket, replacing the original Tin Cat, and we will not switch:</li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].pick(arg[:help].dodge_dupes_4a, 4, 0) %>

<%= header(2, 'Guaranteed uber for the consecutive duplicated rare cats') %>
<ul>
  <li>
    On positions with a consecutive duplicated rare cat, the re-rolled cat
    will also come with a guaranteed uber on guaranteed events.
  </li>
  <li>
    The guaranteed uber you will get on that particular position is
    straightforward. You get the corresponding guaranteed uber depending on
    which cat you get from the position.
  </li>
  <li>
    Here's an example highlighting the path when you get Tin Cat at 3A by
    making 3 single rolls and then make an 11-rolls at 4A on a guaranteed
    event:
    <ol>
      <li>You get 1A, 2A, 3A (Tin Cat) by single rolls.</li>
      <li>Since you get Tin Cat at 3A, the game won't give you another Tin Cat at 4A, you get Pogo Cat at 4AR (4A Re-rolled) instead.</li>
      <li>Then you will switch to track B, and follow through.</li>
      <li>Finally you will switch back to track A after getting the 4ARG (4A Re-rolled Guaranteed) uber.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].guaranteed_on_dupe %>
<ul>
  <li>
    What if your last rolled cat is not a Tin Cat before making 11-rolls
    at 4A on a guaranteed event?
    <ul>
      <li>
        What if you use a platinum ticket at 3A and get Nekoluga, rather than
        Tin Cat? Recall <a href="#dodging-consecutive-duplicated-rare-cat-with-a-platinum-or-legend-ticket">Dodging consecutive duplicated rare cat with a platinum or legend ticket</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Or if it's not a consecutive duplicated rare cat from the same track?
        Recall <a href="#not-necessarily-a-consecutive-duplicated-rare-cat">Not necessarily a consecutive duplicated rare cat</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    Here's an example highlighting the path when you get Nekoluga at 3A by
    making 2 single rolls and 1 platinum roll, and then make an 11-rolls
    at 4A on a guaranteed event:
    <ol>
      <li>You get 1A, 2A by single rolls.</li>
      <li>You get 3A (Nekoluga) by a platinum roll.</li>
      <li>Since you get Nekoluga at 3A, thus your last roll is not a Tin Cat, you get Tin Cat at 4A as usual.</li>
      <li>Then you follow through as usual without switching track.</li>
      <li>Finally you will switch to track B after getting the 4AG (4A Guaranteed) uber completely as usual as if there's no consecutive duplicated rare cat in the first place.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<%= erb :table, cats: arg[:help].guaranteed_on_not_dupe %>

